### sqrt(me^2 + you^2) (without spurious overflow) via libm. Crashes if non-finite.
### :param you: The second leg.
### :returns: The Euclidean length `hypot(me, you)`.
### :throws: {NumericDomainError} when the result is NaN; {NumericOverflowError} on ±inf.
routine D32.hypot!(you: D32) -> D32
  var r = me.hypot_unchecked(you: you)
  if r.is_finite()
    return r
  if r.is_nan()
    throw NumericDomainError(description: "domain error: no real result")
  throw NumericOverflowError(description: "overflow: out of range")

### `hypot(me, you)` via libm double, raw IEEE: may return +inf. Never crashes.
### :param you: The second leg.
### :returns: The Euclidean length, possibly +inf.
routine D32.hypot_unchecked(you: D32) -> D32
  return me.F64().hypot_unchecked(you: you.F64()).D32()

### Fused multiply-add me*b + c, single rounding, via libm. Crashes if non-finite.
### :param b: The multiplier.
### :param c: The addend.
### :returns: `me * b + c` rounded once.
### :throws: {NumericDomainError} when the result is NaN; {NumericOverflowError} on ±inf.
routine D32.fma!(b: D32, c: D32) -> D32
  var r = me.fma_unchecked(b: b, c: c)
  if r.is_finite()
    return r
  if r.is_nan()
    throw NumericDomainError(description: "domain error: no real result")
  throw NumericOverflowError(description: "overflow: out of range")

### `me * b + c` (single rounding) via libm, raw IEEE: may return ±inf or NaN. Never crashes.
